//! The `inset-block` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property defines the logical block start and end offsets of an element, which maps to physical
//! offsets depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation. It
//! corresponds to the `top` and `bottom`, or `right` and `left` properties depending on the values
//! defined for `writing-mode`, `direction`, and `text-orientation`.
//!
//! Initial: inset-block-start: auto; inset-block-end: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: logical-height of containing block.
//!
